// SHA-256's compression function on one block a caller hands whole, as
// compiled code (FIPS 180-4 §6.2.2): `Sha256::compress`, a function of the
// context (`sha256_context.hthr`) that reads the block from a second span.
// The block's bytes are stored where `Sha256::run` wants them, in the
// schedule's first sixteen words, and the block is run. Exported as
// `sha256_compress`.
//
// A module beside `sha256_stream.hthr` and not in it: each calls
// `Sha256::run`, and under the test profile's binary the two together ran
// at the library gate's rail.
import logic;
